{
  "analysis": "Inclusion is the weak class (recall 0.33, 120/179 missed) and the misses are tiny faint vertical streaks (median 33.5px vs 90.5px train; low-size tertile recall only 0.27). Round 2's small-scale any_class pastes lifted it 0.27->0.33, so keep that recipe but raise the floor to 0.4 so pastes stay learnable and add the faint source 287 for the low-contrast misses. Patches (0.65) and scratches (0.56) misses are also small (54px / 42px); scratches actually dropped last round when pushed to 0.3-0.8, so I lift its floor to 0.5-1.0 and restrict to thin line sources (rotation covers the horizontal misses). Patches get a mid-small range and blob sources matching the dark missed blobs. Allocation keeps inclusion below the ~80 diminishing-return zone (70 cumulative) while still feeding the other two classes so the shared detector doesn't starve them.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 20, "patches": 15, "scratches": 15},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 150, 287, 100, 106, 131, 268, 277, 50, 99]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [106, 14, 161, 164, 219, 240, 251, 65, 96, 103, 182, 241]},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.0, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [112, 133, 134, 169, 170, 179, 180, 181, 182, 184, 185, 187, 19, 191, 192, 193, 20, 200, 201, 203, 289, 35, 36, 37, 41, 42, 43, 44, 52, 53, 57, 58, 72, 76, 91, 96]}
  },
  "rationale": "Keep the small-paste strategy that worked for inclusion but with a 0.4 floor for learnability and the faint 287 source; fix scratches' regression by using a 0.5-1.0 range on thin line sources (rotation yields the horizontal misses); give patches mid-small dark-blob pastes. 20/15/15 respects the 50 budget, headroom, the 105 cap, and avoids pushing inclusion past ~80 cumulative."
}

